{"id":"mahabharata-6-077","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":77,"title":"सप्तसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 77 · Seventh day: Bhishma comforts Duryodhana","summary":{"en":"Bhishma cheers the brooding Duryodhana and, with Drona and other great warriors, sets the Kaurava army in a circular array. Arjuna points Krishna to the Trigarta king and his brothers, and routs them.","kn":"ಚಿಂತಿತ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಸಂತೈಸಿ ದ್ರೋಣಾದಿಗಳೊಡನೆ ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ವೃತ್ತವ್ಯೂಹದಲ್ಲಿ ಜೋಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತ್ರಿಗರ್ತರಾಜ ಮತ್ತು ಅವನ ತಮ್ಮಂದಿರನ್ನು ಅರ್ಜುನ ಕೃಷ್ಣನಿಗೆ ತೋರಿಸಿ ಚದುರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म चिन्तित दुर्योधन को प्रोत्साहित करते हैं और द्रोण आदि के साथ कौरव सेना का मण्डल व्यूह बनाते हैं। अर्जुन कृष्ण को त्रिगर्त राजा और उसके भाइयों को दिखाकर उन्हें खदेड़ देते हैं।","te":"చింతలో ఉన్న దుర్యోధనుని భీష్ముడు ఓదార్చి ద్రోణాదులతో కౌరవసేనను మండల వ్యూహంలో నిలుపుతాడు. అర్జునుడు త్రిగర్తరాజును, అతని సోదరులను కృష్ణునికి చూపి వారిని చెదరగొడతాడు.","ta":"கவலையுற்ற துரியோதனனைப் பீஷ்மர் தேற்றி, த்ரோணர் முதலியோருடன் கௌரவப் படையை வட்ட வியூகத்தில் நிறுத்துகிறார். அர்ஜுனன் திரிகர்த்த மன்னனையும் சகோதரரையும் கண்ணனுக்குக் காட்டி அவர்களைச் சிதறடிக்கிறான்.","ml":"ചിന്താകുലനായ ദുര്യോധനനെ ഭീഷ്മർ ആശ്വസിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; ദ്രോണരും മറ്റ് മഹാവീരന്മാരുമായി ചേർന്ന് കൗരവ സേനയെ വൃത്താകൃതിയിലുള്ള വ്യൂഹത്തിൽ നിർത്തുന്നു. ത്രിഗർത്ത രാജാവിനെയും സഹോദരന്മാരെയും ചൂണ്ടിക്കാട്ടി അർജുനൻ കൃഷ്ണനോട് പറയുന്നു; അവരെ തുരത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.77; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथात्मजं तव पुनर्गाङ्गेयो ध्यानमास्थितम् ।\nअब्रवीद्भरतश्रेष्ठः संप्रहर्षकरं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma, son of Ganga and best of the Bharatas, spoke cheering words to your son, who had fallen into brooding."}},{"n":2,"text":"अहं द्रोणश्च शल्यश्च कृतवर्मा च सात्वतः ।\nअश्वत्थामा विकर्णश्च सोमदत्तोऽथ सैन्धवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I, Drona, Shalya, Kritavarman of the Satvatas, Ashvatthama, Vikarna, Somadatta, and Saindhava Jayadratha,"}},{"n":3,"text":"विन्दानुविन्दावावन्त्यौ बाह्लिकः सह बाह्लिकैः ।\nत्रिगर्तराजश्च बली मागधश्च सुदुर्जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Avanti brothers Vinda and Anuvinda, Bahlika with the Bahlikas, the mighty king of the Trigartas, and the hard-to-conquer king of Magadha,"}},{"n":4,"text":"बृहद्बलश्च कौसल्यश्चित्रसेनो विविंशतिः ।\nरथाश्च बहुसाहस्राः शोभमाना महाध्वजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brihadbala of Kosala, Chitrasena, Vivimshati, and many thousands of splendid chariots with great banners,"}},{"n":5,"text":"देशजाश्च हया राजन्स्वारूढा हयसादिभिः ।\nगजेन्द्राश्च मदोद्वृत्ताः प्रभिन्नकरटामुखाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"horses bred in various lands, well ridden by cavalrymen, and great elephants in rut, with temples split and flowing,"}},{"n":6,"text":"पदाताश्च तथा शूरा नानाप्रहरणायुधाः ।\nनानादेशसमुत्पन्नास्त्वदर्थे योद्धुमुद्यताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and brave foot soldiers with weapons of many kinds, born in many lands, are all ready to fight for you."}},{"n":7,"text":"एते चान्ये च बहवस्त्वदर्थे त्यक्तजीविताः ।\nदेवानपि रणे जेतुं समर्था इति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These and many others, who have given up their lives for you, are in my judgment able to defeat even the gods in battle."}},{"n":8,"text":"अवश्यं तु मया राजंस्तव वाच्यं हितं सदा ।\nअशक्याः पाण्डवा जेतुं देवैरपि सवासवैः ।\nवासुदेवसहायाश्च महेन्द्रसमविक्रमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet I must always tell you what is good for you, O king: the Pandavas cannot be conquered even by the gods with Indra, for Vasudeva is their helper and they have the might of great Indra."}},{"n":9,"text":"सर्वथाहं तु राजेन्द्र करिष्ये वचनं तव ।\nपाण्डवान्वा रणे जेष्ये मां वा जेष्यन्ति पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nevertheless, O king of kings, I will do what you ask in every way. Either I will conquer the Pandavas in battle, or the Pandavas will conquer me."}},{"n":10,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ददौ चास्मै विशल्यकरणीं शुभाम् ।\nओषधीं वीर्यसंपन्नां विशल्यश्चाभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, he gave Duryodhana a fine, potent herb that removes arrows, and Duryodhana was then free of his arrows."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततः प्रभाते विमले स्वेनानीकेन वीर्यवान् ।\nअव्यूहत स्वयं व्यूहं भीष्मो व्यूहविशारदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then at bright dawn, mighty Bhishma, skilled in formations, himself arrayed his army in a formation."}},{"n":12,"text":"मण्डलं मनुजश्रेष्ठ नानाशस्त्रसमाकुलम् ।\nसंपूर्णं योधमुख्यैश्च तथा दन्तिपदातिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was a circle, best of men, crowded with weapons of many kinds, full of chief warriors, elephants and foot soldiers,"}},{"n":13,"text":"रथैरनेकसाहस्रैः समन्तात्परिवारितम् ।\nअश्ववृन्दैर्महद्भिश्च ऋष्टितोमरधारिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"surrounded on every side by many thousands of chariots and by great droves of horses bearing spears and lances."}},{"n":14,"text":"नागे नागे रथाः सप्त सप्त चाश्वा रथे रथे ।\nअन्वश्वं दश धानुष्का धानुष्के सप्त चर्मिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For each elephant there were seven chariots, for each chariot seven horses, for each horse ten archers, and for each archer seven shield-bearers."}},{"n":15,"text":"एवंव्यूहं महाराज तव सैन्यं महारथैः ।\nस्थितं रणाय महते भीष्मेण युधि पालितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this formation, O great king, your army stood ready for the great battle with its great chariot-warriors, guarded by Bhishma in the fight."}},{"n":16,"text":"दशाश्वानां सहस्राणि दन्तिनां च तथैव च ।\nरथानामयुतं चापि पुत्राश्च तव दंशिताः ।\nचित्रसेनादयः शूरा अभ्यरक्षन्पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ten thousand horses, as many elephants, a hundred thousand chariots, and your armored sons led by the brave Chitrasena guarded the grandfather."}},{"n":17,"text":"रक्ष्यमाणश्च तैः शूरैर्गोप्यमानाश्च तेन ते ।\nसंनद्धाः समदृश्यन्त राजानश्च महाबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Protected by those heroes and guarded by him, the mighty kings were seen armed and ready."}},{"n":18,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तु समरे दंशितो रथमास्थितः ।\nव्यभ्राजत श्रिया जुष्टो यथा शक्रस्त्रिविष्टपे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, armored and standing on his chariot, shone in the battle with glory, like Indra in heaven."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततः शब्दो महानासीत्पुत्राणां तव भारत ।\nरथघोषश्च तुमुलो वादित्राणां च निस्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O Bharata, a great uproar of your sons rose up, with the din of chariots and the sound of instruments."}},{"n":20,"text":"भीष्मेण धार्तराष्ट्राणां व्यूढः प्रत्यङ्मुखो युधि ।\nमण्डलः सुमहाव्यूहो दुर्भेद्योऽमित्रघातिनाम् ।\nसर्वतः शुशुभे राजन्रणेऽरीणां दुरासदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma had arrayed the Dhritarashtras in a great circle formation facing west, hard for enemy-slayers to break; it shone on every side, O king, and could not be approached by foes in battle."}},{"n":21,"text":"मण्डलं तु समालोक्य व्यूहं परमदारुणम् ।\nस्वयं युधिष्ठिरो राजा व्यूहं वज्रमथाकरोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that circle formation, so terrible, King Yudhishthira himself arrayed his army in the thunderbolt formation."}},{"n":22,"text":"तथा व्यूढेष्वनीकेषु यथास्थानमवस्थिताः ।\nरथिनः सादिनश्चैव सिंहनादमथानदन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the divisions so arrayed and each standing in its place, the charioteers and cavalry raised a lion's roar."}},{"n":23,"text":"बिभित्सवस्ततो व्यूहं निर्ययुर्युद्धकाङ्क्षिणः ।\nइतरेतरतः शूराः सहसैन्याः प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, wishing to break the formation and eager for battle, the warriors with their forces came out from each side to strike."}},{"n":24,"text":"भारद्वाजो ययौ मत्स्यं द्रौणिश्चापि शिखण्डिनम् ।\nस्वयं दुर्योधनो राजा पार्षतं समुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, son of Bharadvaja, went against Virata of Matsya, and Drona's son against Shikhandi. King Duryodhana himself rushed at the son of Prishata, Dhrishtadyumna."}},{"n":25,"text":"नकुलः सहदेवश्च राजन्मद्रेशमीयतुः ।\nविन्दानुविन्दावावन्त्याविरावन्तमभिद्रुतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula and Sahadeva, O king, went against the king of Madra, Shalya, and the Avanti brothers Vinda and Anuvinda charged at Iravan."}},{"n":26,"text":"सर्वे नृपास्तु समरे धनंजयमयोधयन् ।\nभीमसेनो रणे यत्तो हार्दिक्यं समवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kings fought Dhananjaya in the battle, while Bhimasena, intent, held back Kritavarman, son of Hridika."}},{"n":27,"text":"चित्रसेनं विकर्णं च तथा दुर्मर्षणं विभो ।\nआर्जुनिः समरे राजंस्तव पुत्रानयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna's son Abhimanyu fought your sons Chitrasena, Vikarna and Durmarshana in the battle, O lord."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्राग्ज्योतिषं महेष्वासं हैडिम्बो राक्षसोत्तमः ।\nअभिदुद्राव वेगेन मत्तो मत्तमिव द्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghatotkacha, son of Hidimba and best of rakshasas, charged violently at the great bowman Pragjyotisha Bhagadatta, like one rutting elephant at another."}},{"n":29,"text":"अलम्बुसस्ततो राजन्सात्यकिं युद्धदुर्मदम् ।\nससैन्यं समरे क्रुद्धो राक्षसः समभिद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the rakshasa Alambusa, enraged, charged Satyaki, wild in battle, with his army."}},{"n":30,"text":"भूरिश्रवा रणे यत्तो धृष्टकेतुमयोधयत् ।\nश्रुतायुषं तु राजानं धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, intent, fought Dhrishtaketu, while Yudhishthira, the son of Dharma, fought King Shrutayus."}},{"n":31,"text":"चेकितानस्तु समरे कृपमेवान्वयोधयत् ।\nशेषाः प्रतिययुर्यत्ता भीममेव महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chekitana fought Kripa in the battle, and the rest advanced steadily upon the great chariot-warrior Bhima."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततो राजसहस्राणि परिवव्रुर्धनंजयम् ।\nशक्तितोमरनाराचगदापरिघपाणयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then thousands of kings surrounded Dhananjaya, with spears, lances, iron arrows, maces and clubs in their hands."}},{"n":33,"text":"अर्जुनोऽथ भृशं क्रुद्धो वार्ष्णेयमिदमब्रवीत् ।\nपश्य माधव सैन्यानि धार्तराष्ट्रस्य संयुगे ।\nव्यूढानि व्यूहविदुषा गाङ्गेयेन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, greatly angered, said this to Krishna, descendant of Vrishni: See, Madhava, the armies of Dhritarashtra's son drawn up in battle by the great-souled son of Ganga, who knows the formations."}},{"n":34,"text":"युद्धाभिकामाञ्शूरांश्च पश्य माधव दंशितान् ।\nत्रिगर्तराजं सहितं भ्रातृभिः पश्य केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"See these brave men, Madhava, armored and eager to fight. See the king of the Trigartas, Keshava, together with his brothers."}},{"n":35,"text":"अद्यैतान्पातयिष्यामि पश्यतस्ते जनार्दन ।\nय इमे मां यदुश्रेष्ठ योद्धुकामा रणाजिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, Janardana, while you watch, I will bring down those who stand on the field eager to fight me, best of the Yadus."}},{"n":36,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा तु कौन्तेयो धनुर्ज्यामवमृज्य च ।\nववर्ष शरवर्षाणि नराधिपगणान्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken so, the son of Kunti wiped his bowstring and rained showers of arrows on the crowds of kings."}},{"n":37,"text":"तेऽपि तं परमेष्वासाः शरवर्षैरपूरयन् ।\nतडागमिव धाराभिर्यथा प्रावृषि तोयदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They too, great bowmen, filled him with showers of arrows, as clouds in the rainy season fill a pond with their streams."}},{"n":38,"text":"हाहाकारो महानासीत्तव सैन्ये विशां पते ।\nछाद्यमानौ भृशं कृष्णौ शरैर्दृष्ट्वा महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great cry of dismay rose in your army, lord of men, when they saw the two Krishnas heavily covered with arrows in the great battle."}},{"n":39,"text":"देवा देवर्षयश्चैव गन्धर्वाश्च महोरगाः ।\nविस्मयं परमं जग्मुर्दृष्ट्वा कृष्णौ तथागतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods, divine sages, gandharvas and great serpents all fell into deep wonder at seeing the two Krishnas in that plight."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धोऽर्जुनो राजन्नैन्द्रमस्त्रमुदीरयत् ।\nतत्राद्भुतमपश्याम विजयस्य पराक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, Arjuna in anger called up the weapon of Indra. There we saw the marvelous prowess of Vijaya."}},{"n":41,"text":"शस्त्रवृष्टिं परैर्मुक्तां शरौघैर्यदवारयत् ।\nन च तत्राप्यनिर्भिन्नः कश्चिदासीद्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He held off the rain of weapons sent by the enemy with floods of arrows, and not one of them there was left unwounded, O lord of men."}},{"n":42,"text":"तेषां राजसहस्राणां हयानां दन्तिनां तथा ।\nद्वाभ्यां त्रिभिः शरैश्चान्यान्पार्थो विव्याध मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among those thousands of kings and their horses and elephants, Partha pierced some with two arrows and others with three, O revered one."}},{"n":43,"text":"ते हन्यमानाः पार्थेन भीष्मं शांतनवं ययुः ।\nअगाधे मज्जमानानां भीष्मस्त्राताभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down by Partha, they fled to Bhishma, son of Shantanu, who then became the rescuer of those sinking in deep water."}},{"n":44,"text":"आपतद्भिस्तु तैस्तत्र प्रभग्नं तावकं बलम् ।\nसंचुक्षुभे महाराज वातैरिव महार्णवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With them rushing in, your army was broken and tossed, O great king, like the great ocean in storm winds."}}]}]}